 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519063,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Priya takes out unsubsidized student loan, in August, in her first year of college for $2,000. She manages an interest rate of 7%. She graduates after her sixth year of college, in May. She does not pay the interest on the loan during her time in college. What is the balance of her first year loan in May of her graduation year?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The amount due for a loan, <i>A</i>, when the principal, <i>P</i>, an interest rate of <i>r</i> (in decimal form), compounded <i>n</i> times per year for <i>t</i> years is found using the formula <span data-math=\"A = P{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)^{nt}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><i>Hint</i>: Find <i>nt</i> before you plug numbers into your calculator! It will help you get the right results.</p>\n<p><i><span data-math=\"nt = \\left( {12} \\right)\\left( 6 \\right) = 72\"></span></i> if paid the full six years.</p>\n<p>But they are asking for the balance in May when starting in August, so subtract three payments.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"nt = {\\text{ }}72{\\text{ }}-{\\text{ }}3{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}69\"></span></p>\n<p>Use those parentheses in your calculator, too!</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = 2,000{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.07}}{{12}}} \\right)^{69}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = {\\text{ }}\\$ 2,987.63\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$2,987.63"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
